WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.472
Week Three joins vascular access with an introduction to ECGs. The school allocated module Seven G here, including conduction, systematic rhythm checks, twelve-lead views and concerning ischemic patterns.
第3周结合血管通路与心电入门。学校把7G安排在本周，包括传导、系统节律检查、12导联视角及可疑缺血图形。

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:28.680
This first lecture builds a repeatable rhythm method. The next lecture teaches twelve-lead placement, the school three-minute exercise and how recognition leads to communication rather than unsupported independent treatment.
本课先建立可重复的节律方法；下课教授12导联定位、学校三分钟练习，以及如何从识别走向沟通，而不是无依据独立治疗。

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:40.872
We use new synthetic teaching tracings with explicit scales. They demonstrate features and measurements; they are not patient records, a diagnostic simulator or the school assessment strips.
本课采用新绘合成教学记录，并标明比例。它们演示特征及测量，不是患者记录、诊断模拟器或学校考核节律条。

00:00:40.872 --> 00:00:53.376
Keep saying the school questions: what else could this be, what changed after care, what should have changed and what got worse. Do not let an interesting tracing displace immediate patient support.
应持续问学校要求的问题：还可能是什么、照护后变了什么、本来应该怎样变、什么更糟？不能让有趣的心电图挤掉即时患者支持。

00:00:53.376 --> 00:01:05.832
An ECG records electrical potential differences between skin electrodes. It does not directly show blood pressure, stroke volume, coronary anatomy or whether a palpable pulse exists.
心电图记录皮肤电极之间的电位差，不直接显示血压、搏出量、冠脉解剖，也不能证明有可触脉搏。

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:18.816
Assess responsiveness, breathing and circulation using the trained primary assessment. Organized electrical complexes with no detectable pulse can represent pulseless electrical activity.
应按受训初评检查反应、呼吸及循环。有组织电活动但检测不到脉搏，可代表无脉电活动。

00:01:18.816 --> 00:01:32.256
Conversely, a talking person with an apparent chaotic monitor trace may have artifact. Assess the patient and equipment promptly without assuming every unusual waveform is ventricular fibrillation.
相反，正在说话者监护图形混乱，可能是伪差。须及时检查患者及器材，不能把每种异常波形都认成室颤。

00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:42.888
Use the monitor to add evidence to care. Never delay indicated resuscitation to complete a six-step description or obtain the perfect twelve-lead printout.
监护仪应为照护增加证据。不能为完成六步描述或取得完美12导联，延误有指征的复苏。

00:01:42.888 --> 00:01:54.432
In usual sinus activation, the sinoatrial node in the right atrium initiates an impulse. Activation spreads through atrial tissue toward the atrioventricular junction.
通常窦性激动由右心房窦房结发出冲动，激动经心房组织向房室交界传播。

00:01:54.432 --> 00:02:06.960
The AV junction introduces a delay before activation passes into the His bundle, bundle branches and Purkinje network. That sequence helps coordinate filling and ventricular activation.
房室交界产生延迟，之后激动进入希氏束、束支及浦肯野网络。这个顺序有助协调充盈及心室激动。

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:19.992
A delay or an alternative route can change timing and QRS appearance. The strip is a surface consequence of electrical activity, not a photograph of exactly where an abnormal impulse began.
延迟或替代通路可改变时间及QRS形态。体表记录是电活动的结果，不是异常冲动确切起点的照片。

00:02:19.992 --> 00:02:28.824
Trace the pathway aloud while looking at the figure, then identify which measured event would change if atrioventricular conduction slowed.
看图大声说出传导路径，再指出房室传导变慢时，哪项测量会改变。

00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:39.576
Automaticity means some specialized cells can depolarize spontaneously. A slower backup focus may emerge when faster impulses no longer drive the system.
自律性是某些特殊细胞能自行除极。当较快冲动不再驱动系统时，较慢的后备起搏灶可能出现。

00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:50.400
The school gives typical adult teaching ranges of sixty to one hundred for sinus activity, forty to sixty for junctional escape and twenty to forty for ventricular escape.
学校给出的成人典型教学范围是：窦性每分钟60至100次，交界性逸搏40至60次，心室逸搏20至40次。

00:02:50.400 --> 00:03:04.128
These ranges overlap with disease, medicines and physiological variation. A rate alone does not identify a focus, and a backup electrical rhythm may still fail to provide effective circulation.
疾病、药物及生理变异会影响这些范围。单看速度不能定位起搏灶；后备电节律也可能无法维持有效循环。

00:03:04.128 --> 00:03:15.192
Assess the relation between rate and symptoms: new confusion, syncope, chest discomfort or poor perfusion matters more than simply labelling a number slow.
要评速度与症状的关系。新意识混乱、晕厥、胸部不适或灌注差，比只把某个数字叫作慢更重要。

00:03:15.192 --> 00:03:29.304
Depolarization changes the electrical state of myocardial cells; repolarization is their electrical recovery. These processes are related to contraction and relaxation but are not identical to them.
除极改变心肌细胞电状态，复极是电恢复。它们与收缩、舒张有关，但并不完全等同。

00:03:29.304 --> 00:03:42.456
When a net electrical vector moves toward a positive viewing electrode, the deflection often points upward; movement away can produce a negative deflection. The same event can look different in another lead.
净电向量朝向正观察电极时，波形常向上；远离时可向下。同一次活动在另一导联可能呈不同外观。

00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:53.928
Do not interpret an upward waveform as good blood flow or a downward waveform as a failed beat. Direction describes a view, not the clinical success of the contraction.
不能把向上波形理解为血流好，或向下波形理解为失败心搏。方向描述的是视角，不是收缩的临床成功与否。

00:03:53.928 --> 00:04:04.344
A lead is a calculated view, while an electrode is a physical sensor. That distinction explains how ten electrodes can provide twelve views in the next lecture.
导联是计算得到的视角，电极是实体传感器。这个区别解释了下课中十个电极如何提供十二个视角。

00:04:04.344 --> 00:04:15.576
The P wave represents atrial depolarization. The QRS complex represents ventricular depolarization, and the T wave represents ventricular repolarization.
P波代表心房除极，QRS波群代表心室除极，T波代表心室复极。

00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:28.920
A Q wave is an initial negative deflection before an R wave, R is a positive deflection and S is a negative deflection after R. Not every normal complex contains all three named components.
Q是R前最初负向波，R为正向波，S为R后负向波。正常波群未必都能看见这三个组成。

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:41.424
Identify the actual onset of the QRS, not simply the tall R peak, when measuring PR, QRS or QT. An absent visible Q does not prevent measuring those intervals.
测PR、QRS或QT时，应找QRS真实起点，不能只找高耸R峰。看不见Q波，也仍然可以测这些间期。

00:04:41.424 --> 00:04:52.944
Use a clear baseline and a lead with visible boundaries. If motion or overlapping waves obscure a boundary, state uncertainty rather than inventing precision.
应选基线清楚、边界可见的导联。移动或波形重叠遮住边界时，要说明不确定，不能编造精度。

00:04:52.944 --> 00:05:04.128
At twenty-five millimetres per second, one millimetre horizontally represents zero point zero four seconds, and five small boxes represent zero point two seconds.
走纸速度25毫米每秒时，横向一毫米代表0.04秒，五小格代表0.20秒。

00:05:04.128 --> 00:05:14.544
At the usual gain of ten millimetres per millivolt, vertical height represents voltage. Horizontal time and vertical voltage answer different questions.
通常增益为每毫伏10毫米，纵向高度代表电压。横向时间和纵向电压回答不同问题。

00:05:14.544 --> 00:05:24.816
A changed paper speed or gain changes the meaning of a box. Always inspect the actual printout settings rather than applying a memorized value to every display.
走纸速度或增益改变后，每格意义也改变。必须检查实际记录设置，不能把背下的格值套到所有屏幕。

00:05:24.816 --> 00:05:36.552
Our six-second figures explicitly use the standard represented scale. Browser zoom changes physical screen size, not the labelled time relationships in the authored diagram.
本课六秒图示明确采用所标标准比例。浏览器缩放会改变屏幕尺寸，但不会改变图中标明的时间关系。

00:05:36.552 --> 00:05:50.304
PR starts at the beginning of P and ends at the beginning of QRS. The usual adult reference is zero point one two to zero point two zero seconds, or three to five small boxes at standard speed.
PR从P起点量到QRS起点。通常成人参考为0.12至0.20秒，即标准速度下三至五小格。

00:05:50.304 --> 00:06:03.840
QRS width includes the whole ventricular depolarization complex, not only the R wave. A width of zero point one two seconds or more is classified as wide in this introductory rhythm method.
QRS宽度包括整个心室除极波群，不仅R波。本入门方法把0.12秒或以上归为宽QRS。

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:15.960
The ST segment begins at the J point, where QRS ends. QT continues from QRS onset through the end of T, including depolarization and repolarization.
ST段从QRS结束处的J点开始。QT从QRS起点一直到T波结束，包含心室除极与复极。

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:29.304
The saved school table contains inconsistent decimal values such as a zero point eight second P wave. Do not memorize those typographical values; use the verified landmarks and measurements taught here.
学校存档表内有不一致小数，例如把P波写成0.8秒。不要背这些排印值，应采用这里核实的标志及测量。

00:06:29.304 --> 00:06:41.064
QT is not one fixed normal number for every heart rate and person. Rate correction and the method used matter, as do difficult T-wave boundaries and a wide QRS.
QT并非对所有心率及所有人都有一个固定正常值。心率校正及所用方法很重要，T波边界不清和宽QRS也会影响解释。

00:06:41.064 --> 00:06:54.240
A prolonged repolarization concern may relate to medications, electrolyte disturbances or inherited conditions. A machine flag is a reason for review, not a complete causal diagnosis.
复极延长可能与药物、电解质或遗传情况有关。机器提示值得复核，但不能单独完成病因诊断。

00:06:54.240 --> 00:07:05.856
Do not calculate a correction from a poor tracing and treat its apparent precision as certainty. Record the measured findings, settings and symptoms and seek the appropriate support.
不能从差记录算出校正值后，就把表面精度当作确定。应记录测量、设置及症状，并取得适当支持。

00:07:05.856 --> 00:07:18.216
The practical goal today is accurate acquisition and recognition of a concern. Specialist risk calculation does not replace assessing syncope, instability or a dangerous rhythm now.
今天的实用目标是准确采集并识别疑点。专科风险计算不能替代对当前晕厥、不稳定或危险节律的评估。

00:07:18.216 --> 00:07:28.464
Explain the procedure, obtain appropriate consent and expose only what is needed. Support the patient and limbs in a clinically tolerable position.
解释操作，取得适当同意，只暴露所需部位，并以患者临床可耐受体位支撑身体和肢体。

00:07:28.464 --> 00:07:39.096
Prepare skin and electrode contact using the trained method. Sweat, hair, poor adhesion, cold or a damaged cable can impair the signal.
按受训方法准备皮肤和电极接触。汗、毛发、贴合不良、寒冷或线缆损坏，都可影响信号。

00:07:39.096 --> 00:07:49.848
Verify the physical labels instead of assuming every manufacturer uses the same colour code. Keep cable tension and unnecessary movement out of the recording.
应核实体标签，不能假定所有厂商使用相同颜色。记录时要减少线缆牵拉和不必要移动。

00:07:49.848 --> 00:07:59.976
Ask for a brief quiet recording with normal breathing when possible. Check the result rather than assuming that a successful print means a diagnostically useful signal.
可行时请患者正常呼吸，短暂安静记录。打印成功不代表信号具有诊断价值，仍须检查结果。

00:07:59.976 --> 00:08:11.400
Movement, tremor, muscle activity, loose contact and electrical interference can imitate disease. First compare the tracing with the person's actual clinical state.
移动、震颤、肌肉活动、接触松动及电干扰都可模仿疾病。首先应把图形与患者真实状态对照。

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:23.328
Look across available leads and for regular complexes continuing through the noise. Check the cable and contact, reduce a reversible noise source and reassess the signal.
比较可用导联，寻找噪声中仍持续出现的规则波群。检查线缆和接触，减少可逆噪声，再核信号。

00:08:23.328 --> 00:08:35.688
A comfortable talking patient and apparent VF strongly demand a signal check. An unresponsive pulseless patient demands the arrest pathway while appropriate equipment checks occur.
舒适且能说话者看似室颤，强烈要求查信号；无反应无脉者则要进入骤停路径，同时作适当器材检查。

00:08:35.688 --> 00:08:47.712
Do not label every unexpected finding artifact. If it persists with a good signal, describe it and obtain review; if the clinical condition worsens, respond to that immediately.
不能把所有意外所见都叫伪差。好信号下仍存在时，应描述并寻求复核；临床恶化则立即响应。

00:08:47.712 --> 00:08:58.752
After confirming patient priority and signal quality, calculate rate and assess regularity. Then inspect P waves and their relationship to QRS complexes.
确认患者优先事项及信号质量后，算速度、看规则性，再检查P波及其与QRS的关系。

00:08:58.752 --> 00:09:08.664
Measure PR where it is measurable and measure the full QRS width. Finish with a scan for concerning ST-T findings that may require a twelve-lead view.
能够测量时测PR，并测完整QRS宽度。最后扫查可疑ST-T变化，判断是否需要12导联视角。

00:09:08.664 --> 00:09:19.080
Synthesize the observations rather than jumping to a label after the first feature. A rate of one hundred and fifty does not alone establish the rhythm origin.
要综合观察，不能见到首个特征就贴标签。每分钟150次本身不能确定节律起源。

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:29.760
State what you see, what you cannot assess and the clinical consequence. This method supports recognition and escalation within actual training and authorization.
说出看见什么、无法评什么，以及临床后果。这套方法支持在真实训练和权限内识别并升级处理。

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:40.344
At standard speed, a regular rhythm with four large boxes between R peaks has an estimated rate of three hundred divided by four, or seventy-five per minute.
标准速度下，规则节律R峰之间四大格，估计心率为300除4，即每分钟75次。

00:09:40.344 --> 00:09:52.392
For an irregular rhythm, count QRS complexes in a known six-second interval and multiply by ten for an approximate average. Boundary and short-sample effects limit precision.
不规则节律可在已知六秒范围内数QRS再乘十，得到近似平均。边界及短样本效应会限制精度。

00:09:52.392 --> 00:10:03.888
A monitor can double-count tall T waves or miss low complexes. Compare its rate with your tracing calculation and clinical pulse rather than copying the display uncritically.
监护仪可能重复数高T波，或漏数低波群。应与自己算的速度及临床脉搏比较，不能照抄显示值。

00:10:03.888 --> 00:10:13.992
In atrial-ventricular dissociation, atrial and ventricular rates can differ. For perfusion-related reasoning, make clear which rate you are reporting.
房室分离时，房率和室率可能不同。作灌注相关推理时，要说清报告的是哪个速度。

00:10:13.992 --> 00:10:23.064
Compare successive R-to-R intervals across enough of the strip. Calipers or a paper edge can make a subtle pattern easier to see.
沿足够长的记录比较连续R-R间期。卡尺或纸边可帮助看出细微模式。

00:10:23.064 --> 00:10:32.856
A repeating irregular pattern differs from a rhythm with no repeating interval sequence. That description helps the receiving clinician understand the evidence.
重复出现的不齐，与没有重复间期序列的节律不同。这样描述能让接收者理解证据。

00:10:32.856 --> 00:10:43.320
Check whether apparent variation comes from motion, missed complexes or a very short sample. A longer strip or another lead may clarify the pattern.
要检查表面变化是否来自移动、漏波或样本太短。较长记录或另一导联可能更清楚。

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:54.840
Regularity alone does not determine safety. A regular rhythm can be dangerously fast or slow, while an irregular rhythm can still have a pulse and require non-arrest assessment.
规则性不能单独决定安全。规则节律也可危险地过快过慢；不齐节律也可能有脉，需要非骤停评估。

00:10:54.840 --> 00:11:21.432
The assigned nursing video offers a useful six-step rhythm method, but a shortcut is only valid under its assumptions. In this original ten-second example, twelve identifiable ventricular complexes give an estimated rate of seventy-two per minute. Do not multiply by ten unless the measured strip really spans six seconds. Check speed, signal and actual duration before defending a number.
指定护理视频提供有用的六步心律方法，但捷径只在假设成立时有效。本原创十秒例中，十二个可识别心室波群，估计每分钟72次。只有记录真实时长为六秒才能乘十。应先核纸速、信号及真实时长，不能先维护一个数字。

00:11:21.432 --> 00:11:47.328
Then explain the patient, not only the strip. Assess perfusion and symptoms, describe P waves and their relationship to the ventricular complexes, and measure the relevant intervals. A normal-looking rate does not prove useful circulation. This rhythm sequence must not exclude ST or QT assessment when the clinical problem requires them, and it does not replace the separate twelve-lead acquisition lesson.
随后应解释患者，不能只解释纸条。评估灌注及症状，描述P波及其与心室波群的关系，并测相关间期。频率看似正常，不证明循环有用。临床问题需要时，该心律顺序不能排除ST或QT评估，也不能替代独立的十二导联采集课。

00:11:47.328 --> 00:11:58.992
In a usual sinus pattern, similar P waves precede each QRS and have an appropriate relationship to ventricular activation. Lead orientation changes their appearance.
通常窦性模式中，相似P波先于每个QRS，并与心室激动有适当关系。导联方向会改变外观。

00:11:58.992 --> 00:12:11.112
Look for extra atrial activity, P waves not followed by QRS or QRS complexes without a clearly preceding P. Count relationships rather than assuming one bump means normal.
要找额外房性活动、P后无QRS，或QRS前没有清楚P。应数关系，不能见到一个小凸起就认作正常。

00:12:11.112 --> 00:12:24.264
At fast rates or with low amplitude, a P may be buried in another wave. The school's simple missing-P rule cannot prove that sinus origin is excluded in every noisy or fast tracing.
速度快或波幅低时，P可能埋在其他波中。学校简单的无P规则，不能证明所有噪声或快节律都排除窦性起源。

00:12:24.264 --> 00:12:34.728
If a P cannot be identified reliably, report that it is not clearly visible. Seek a better lead or review rather than inventing a PR interval.
无法可靠辨P时，应报告P不清晰。寻找更好导联或复核，不能编一个PR。

00:12:34.728 --> 00:12:46.776
Measure from the first P deflection to the first QRS deflection. A prolonged PR indicates delayed atrioventricular conduction but does not by itself precisely locate the delay.
应从P第一次偏离基线量到QRS第一次偏离。PR延长提示房室传导延迟，但不能独自精确定位延迟部位。

00:12:46.776 --> 00:12:57.192
Examine more than one beat. A changing interval, extra P waves or dropped QRS complexes provides different evidence from a consistently long interval.
应看不止一搏。间期变化、额外P或QRS脱落，与持续固定长PR提供的是不同证据。

00:12:57.192 --> 00:13:09.576
A short PR can have several explanations. Do not diagnose a specific accessory pathway solely from one short interval without the other features and appropriate expertise.
短PR有多种解释。没有其他特征和适当专业判断，不能只凭一个短间期诊断特定旁路。

00:13:09.576 --> 00:13:22.032
For today, describe the measured relationship and patient condition. Symptomatic poor perfusion or a concerning block pattern needs prompt escalation rather than a long naming exercise.
今天先描述测得关系和患者状态。症状性低灌注或可疑阻滞模式需要及时升级，不能长时间只练命名。

00:13:22.032 --> 00:13:33.024
Measure the complete QRS from onset to end in a lead with clear boundaries. At standard speed, three small boxes represent zero point one two seconds.
在边界清楚的导联中，从起点到终点测完整QRS。标准速度下，三小格为0.12秒。

00:13:33.024 --> 00:13:43.056
A narrow complex commonly reflects activation through a relatively rapid ventricular conduction route. It does not prove that every upstream process is normal.
窄波群通常反映心室经相对快速路径激动，但不能证明上游所有过程正常。

00:13:43.056 --> 00:13:55.560
A wide complex can arise from ventricular origin, bundle-branch conduction delay, pacing or other effects. Do not use wide equals ventricular as a universal diagnostic equation.
宽波群可来自心室起源、束支传导延迟、起搏或其他影响。不能把宽等于室性当作通用诊断公式。

00:13:55.560 --> 00:14:08.496
A rapid wide-complex pattern is potentially dangerous. Assess pulse and instability, obtain appropriate support and use the actual authorized pathway rather than guessing a drug from width.
快速宽波模式可能危险。应评脉搏及不稳定，取得适当支持，遵真实获准路径，不能凭宽度猜药。

00:14:08.496 --> 00:14:21.024
Identify the baseline and J point before describing ST displacement. Noise, QRS conduction abnormalities and the selected lead can make a quick single-strip judgment unreliable.
描述ST移位前，先认基线和J点。噪声、QRS传导异常及所选导联，都可使快速单条判读不可靠。

00:14:21.024 --> 00:14:33.696
Notice clear elevation, depression or concerning T-wave changes and obtain the appropriate twelve-lead view and review. The next lecture teaches lead groupings and the qualified criteria.
明显抬高、压低或可疑T波变化时，应取得适当12导联并复核。下课会讲导联分组及有条件的标准。

00:14:33.696 --> 00:14:46.032
Do not apply the school shortcut of two millimetres in every chest lead. Criteria depend on the actual lead and, particularly for V two and V three, patient category.
不能采用所有胸导联都两毫米的学校捷径。标准取决于真实导联，尤其V2、V3还取决于患者类别。

00:14:46.032 --> 00:14:57.576
A clean normal strip does not rule out coronary ischemia or another dangerous cause of symptoms. Continue assessment, repeat when indicated and communicate the full clinical picture.
清楚正常的节律条，不能排除冠脉缺血或其他危险病因。应继续评估、按需复查，并交代完整临床情况。

00:14:57.576 --> 00:15:08.184
Figure A has six QRS complexes over six seconds and a one-second R-to-R interval. Both methods give sixty per minute in this teaching strip.
A图六秒内有六个QRS，R-R为一秒；两种算法在这张教学记录中都得每分钟60次。

00:15:08.184 --> 00:15:18.168
Similar visible P waves precede each narrow QRS with a consistent relationship. That supports a usual sinus description in this schematic.
每个窄QRS之前都有相似可见P，关系一致，支持在本示意图中描述为通常窦性模式。

00:15:18.168 --> 00:15:30.264
The same person could still have coronary ischemia, bleeding, sepsis or another problem. A baseline rhythm is not proof of stable physiology or absence of a treatment indication.
同一人仍可能有冠脉缺血、出血、脓毒症或其他问题。基础节律不能证明生理稳定，也不能排除治疗适应证。

00:15:30.264 --> 00:15:37.896
Say the rhythm findings, then say how the patient is doing. Those are related but separate parts of a meaningful report.
应先说节律所见，再说患者状态。二者相关，但在有意义的报告中是不同部分。

00:15:37.896 --> 00:15:48.048
The slow teaching strip has a one-and-a-half-second R-to-R interval, corresponding to forty per minute. Now add the patient information before judging urgency.
慢节律图R-R为1.5秒，对应每分钟40次。判断紧迫性前，必须加入患者信息。

00:15:48.048 --> 00:15:58.968
A well person with a known low baseline differs from someone with new faintness, chest pressure and poor perfusion. Do not treat the number without the clinical consequence.
已知基础心率低但状态好的人，与新头晕、胸压和灌注差者不同。不能不看临床后果就只治数字。

00:15:58.968 --> 00:16:12.480
Review oxygenation, ventilation, circulation, medication effects and other plausible causes while providing necessary support. A sinus label does not make symptomatic bradycardia harmless.
提供必要支持时，应复核氧合、通气、循环、药物及其他可能原因。窦性标签不能让症状性心动过缓变无害。

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:26.280
Report the onset, symptoms, pulse, blood pressure trend and ECG relationship. This lesson does not authorize independent pacing or an advanced drug merely because the rate is low.
应报告发作、症状、脉搏、血压趋势及心电关系。本课不因心率低就授权独立起搏或高级用药。

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:37.752
A rapid rate may compensate for another problem or arise from a primary rhythm disturbance. Treating every fast number as an isolated rhythm problem risks missing the cause.
速度快可能是在代偿其他问题，也可能来自原发节律异常。把所有快心率当作孤立节律问题，会漏掉病因。

00:16:37.752 --> 00:16:48.720
Describe whether it is regular, whether P waves can be assessed and whether QRS is narrow or wide. Then integrate onset, symptoms and perfusion.
应描述是否规则、P能否评估、QRS窄或宽，再结合发作、症状及灌注。

00:16:48.720 --> 00:17:00.936
Consider plausible causes such as pain, fever, volume loss, medication or substance effects, and do not dismiss a sick patient as anxious without appropriate assessment.
考虑疼痛、发热、失液、药物或物质作用等原因。不能未经适当评估，就把病重者打发成焦虑。

00:17:00.936 --> 00:17:12.000
Provide indicated supportive care and obtain the appropriate clinical review. A memorized label is not authorization for an antiarrhythmic or a shock in a patient with a pulse.
应提供有指征的支持并取得适当临床复核。背下名称不等于获准给抗心律失常药，或给有脉患者电击。

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:22.224
This new schematic has unequal intervals and no clearly consistent P waves. Those are the observed features, not a complete patient diagnosis.
这张新示意图的间期不等，P波也没有清楚一致性。这些只是观察特征，不是完整患者诊断。

00:17:22.224 --> 00:17:32.208
An irregularly irregular ventricular response without consistent P waves can suggest atrial fibrillation, but a short or noisy sample can mislead.
无一致P波、室律绝对不齐可提示房颤，但短记录或噪声可使人误判。

00:17:32.208 --> 00:17:41.592
Seek a useful longer strip or other lead when appropriate, check whether the pulse and monitor agree and assess symptoms, rate and perfusion.
适当时应取得有用的较长记录或另一导联，核脉搏与监护是否一致，并评症状、速度和灌注。

00:17:41.592 --> 00:17:53.640
Do not infer the duration of the rhythm, anticoagulation need or a safe discharge decision from this introductory pattern. Communicate findings and obtain the actual authorized review.
不能从这个入门图形推断持续时间、抗凝需求或安全出院。应交代所见，并获得真实获准的复核。

00:17:53.640 --> 00:18:05.928
A ventricular tachycardia pattern commonly appears as rapid wide complexes. It can occur with a pulse or without one; that distinction cannot be made by the tracing alone.
室速模式常为快速宽波群，可有脉也可无脉。单靠图形无法作出这个区别。

00:18:05.928 --> 00:18:18.360
Pulseless VT and ventricular fibrillation are shockable arrest rhythms. Follow the trained arrest and AED or authorized defibrillator sequence while maintaining high-quality resuscitation.
无脉室速和室颤属于可电击骤停节律。应遵受训骤停及AED或获准除颤流程，并保持高质量复苏。

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:28.512
VF lacks organized, identifiable QRS complexes. Check the clinical state, because movement artifact can resemble it in a perfusing patient.
室颤缺乏有组织、可辨认的QRS。仍要查临床状态，因为灌注良好者的移动伪差可能看起来相似。

00:18:28.512 --> 00:18:39.864
Do not give an unsynchronized arrest shock to a conscious perfusing patient merely because the screen is wide and fast. Obtain immediate appropriate support for instability.
不能只因屏幕宽而快，就给清醒且有灌注者非同步骤停电击。不稳定时应立即取得适当支持。

00:18:39.864 --> 00:18:54.336
An apparent flatline may be asystole, but disconnected leads, the selected view or equipment settings can create a misleading display. Verify appropriately without prolonging interruptions in necessary resuscitation.
平线可能是心室停搏，也可能由导联断开、所选视角或器材设置造成。应适当核查，但不能延长必要复苏中断。

00:18:54.336 --> 00:19:06.360
Ventricular asystole means absent detectable ventricular activity and can occasionally coexist with atrial activity. It is not made shockable by increasing monitor gain.
心室停搏表示检测不到心室电活动，偶尔仍可伴房性活动。调大增益不会让它变成可电击节律。

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:18.552
PEA is a clinical combination of organized electrical activity and no detectable pulse. It can look like an ordinary rhythm on paper; assessment of circulation is essential.
PEA是有组织电活动加检测不到脉搏的临床组合。纸面可能看似普通节律，因此必须检查循环。

00:19:18.552 --> 00:19:31.272
Both require the actual non-shockable arrest pathway and attention to reversible causes. Complete resuscitation team procedures are developed further in the school cardiac-resuscitation weekend.
二者都需遵真实不可电击骤停路径，并关注可逆原因。学校心脏复苏周会进一步发展完整团队流程。

00:19:31.272 --> 00:19:41.472
In this original example, four large boxes between R peaks gives seventy-five per minute. Consistent spacing means the sampled rhythm is regular.
本原创例R峰间四大格，得每分钟75次；间隔一致，表示这段样本规则。

00:19:41.472 --> 00:19:51.936
Four small boxes for PR gives zero point one six seconds. Two small boxes for QRS gives zero point zero eight seconds, a narrow complex.
PR四小格为0.16秒，QRS两小格为0.08秒，属于窄波群。

00:19:51.936 --> 00:20:05.640
Similar P waves preceding each QRS with that relationship supports a sinus description. It does not answer whether the patient's chest pressure is coronary, vascular, pulmonary or another problem.
相似P先于每个QRS并有上述关系，支持窦性描述。但不能回答患者胸压究竟是冠脉、血管、肺或其他问题。

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:17.160
Continue the primary assessment, obtain the appropriate twelve-lead and consider alternatives while care proceeds. A regular rhythm at seventy-five is not a clearance test.
应继续初评、取得适当12导联，并在照护中考虑替代解释。每分钟75次的规则节律不是排除危险的通行证。

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:28.320
Without reading the slide, trace the conduction pathway and name the electrical meaning of P, QRS and T. Explain why none independently proves a pulse.
不看课件，讲出传导路径及P、QRS、T的电学意义，并解释为什么它们都不能单独证明有脉。

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:39.912
Calculate the rate for three, four and five large boxes between regular R peaks, then convert four small boxes to seconds. State which settings must be verified first.
算规则R峰间三、四、五大格的心率，再把四小格换成秒，并说出应先核哪些设置。

00:20:39.912 --> 00:20:53.424
Compare rapid wide-complex activity with and without a pulse, then organized activity with and without a pulse. Explain the change in urgency and pathway without inventing new permissions.
比较快宽波有脉与无脉，以及有组织活动有脉与无脉。说明紧迫性和路径变化，不能自创新权限。

00:20:53.424 --> 00:21:05.784
Take the same disciplined observation into the next lesson: ten correctly placed electrodes, a readable twelve-lead, rapid communication and reassessment after every intervention.
带着同样严谨观察进入下课：十个电极正确定位，12导联可读，迅速沟通，并在每次干预后复评。
